Checkpoint. For s: String and v: Vec<i32>, what types are *s and *v?
   *s : str
   *v : [i32]

Each owned type names its borrowed half as Deref::Target
   String   -> str
   Vec<i32> -> [i32]
   PathBuf  -> std::path::Path

Lending the borrowed half copies nothing: same bytes, shorter handle
   &s as &str   = "Ada", same bytes as s: true
   &v as &[i32] = [1, 2, 3], same bytes as v: true
   &p as &Path  = "notes.txt"

Going the other way has to build a new owner
   bs.to_owned() = "Ada", same bytes as s: false
